  "notes": [
    "Impersonal/defective -AR verb with e→ie stem change; in natural usage only the 3rd person singular is used (*nieva* = it is snowing)",
    "Stem change applies in presente (all forms except nosotros/nosotras): *nieve, nievas, nieva, nievan*",
    "No stem change in pretérito indefinido (-AR verbs never change in preterite)",
    "Subjuntivo nosotros reverts to infinitive stem: *nevemos* (not *\\*nievemos*)",
    "Past participle: nevado (regular)",
    "*Está nevando* = It is snowing (progressive, more common than *nieva* for ongoing action)",
    "*Nevó mucho este invierno* = It snowed a lot this winter",
    "Related: la nieve (snow), el copo de nieve (snowflake), neviscar (to sleet/drizzle snow), llover (to rain)"
  ],
